¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙeTherefore thou shalt keep the commandments of the LORD thy God, to walk in his ways, and to fear him.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙFor the LORD thy God bringeth thee into a good land, a land of brooks of water, of fountains and depths that spring out of valleys and hills;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙha land of wheat, and barley, and vines, and fig trees, and pomegranates; a land of oil olive, and honey;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse	¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¨a land wherein thou shalt eat bread without scarceness, thou shalt not lack any thing in it; a land whose stones are iron, and out of whose hills thou mayest dig brass.¦layout ªlast_verse	„¥verse
